es without fabricating credentials or social proof."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/identity.css"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/images/portfolio-icon-180.png"><link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"></head><body data-page="personal-branding-and-online-identity.html" class="academy page-lesson master-refresh"><header class="academy-header" id="top"><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><button class="academy-menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="academy-nav">Menu <span>+</span></button><nav id="academy-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href='/about'>About</a><a href='/projects'>Projects</a><a href='/services'>Services</a><a class='header-cta' href='/hire-me'>Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="portfolio-more"><summary>More</summary><div class="portfolio-panel"><section><h2>Professional work</h2><a href='/case-studies'>Case Studies</a><a href='/changelog'>Projects Changelog</a><a href='/delivered-project'>Process</a><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/news'>Notes</a></section><section><h2>Contact &amp; career</h2><a href='/book-a-call'>Book a Call</a><a href='/resume'>Resume / CV</a><a href='/hire-me'>Hire Me</a></section><section><h2>Content &amp; media</h2><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/blog'>Blog &amp; Articles</a><a href='/faq'>FAQs</a></section><section><h2>Personal brand</h2><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Founder Profile</a><a href='/social'>Social Profiles</a><a href='/official-links'>Official Links</a></section></div></details><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch color theme">◐</button></nav></header>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
<main class="container academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/blog'>Learning library</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">lesson <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1>Personal Branding and Online Identity</h1><p>A credible professional presence helps people understand who you are, what you work on and how they can verify or contact you. Consistency matters more than creating profiles on every platform.</p></section><div class="academy-reading-layout"><aside class="academy-toc"><p class="academy-kicker">IN THIS GUIDE</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#section-1"><span>01</span>Keep identity details consistent</a><a href="#section-2"><span>02</span>Show work with context</a><a href="#section-3"><span>03</span>Use evidence, not inflated claims</a><a href="#section-4"><span>04</span>Make contact pathways clear</a><a href="#section-5"><span>05</span>Maintain the profile over time</a></nav><div class="academy-author"><img src="/assets/images/mbk-personal-favicon-96.png" width="38" height="38" alt=""><div>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Founder, MBK Global</small></div></div><p class="academy-read-note">2 min read · Practical learning notes<br>Learn. Apply. Make it your own.</p><a class='academy-text-link' href='/resources'>More learning resources ↗</a></aside><div class="academy-reading-body"><article class="content-page"><header><p class="eyebrow">MBK Global · Practical guide</p></header><section><h2 id="section-1">Keep identity details consistent</h2><p>Use the same preferred name, role descriptions, brand name and canonical website across profiles where you actively participate. Keep a single source of truth for public links and update outdated references when the production host changes.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-2">Show work with context</h2><p>For each project, explain the problem, your contribution, technologies used and current status. Link to a working demo or repository only when it is genuinely available. Distinguish experiments and learning projects from paid client work.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-3">Use evidence, not inflated claims</h2><p>Do not publish invented client names, testimonials, awards, metrics or qualifications. If you are still building experience, describe the actual skills and projects you can demonstrate and identify areas you are continuing to learn.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-4">Make contact pathways clear</h2><p>Keep contact, booking and social links current and test them periodically. Explain what information a form collects and avoid requesting sensitive details that are not necessary. Never publish private contact data without considering the consequences.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-5">Maintain the profile over time</h2><p>Review your portfolio after meaningful project changes, remove broken links and keep descriptions factual. Create profiles only on services you intend to maintain; low-quality mass profile creation can damage trust rather than build it.</p></section>
<p><strong>About this guide:</strong> This is general educational guidance. Adapt recommendations to your site's actual stack, risk and audience, and verify changes before publishing.</p>
<p>Explore related work: <a href='/web-development'>web development</a>, <a href='/projects'>projects</a>, and <a href='/contact'>contact</a>.</p></article></div></div><div data-portrait-track data-caption="A personal archive / Bakhtawar Khan"></div></main>
